FINAL ANSWER:
## Who owns the code today

Ownership here is surviving lines from `git blame` at HEAD, not commit counts. I ran `blame` with `-w -M -C` and `--ignore-rev 62628c0`. That commit is the 4-space/double-quote reformat. It touched 1016 lines, so without the exclusion it would own most of the repo.

Scope is the 7 tracked JS files, 1,202 lines. `lib/index.js` has 238 lines and `test/test.js` has 731. I merged `alex94puchades` into Alejandro Caravaca Puchades. I did not merge the two `Troy Goode` emails, because `blame` already reports them under one name.

| Owner | Surviving lines | Share | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 676 | 56% | 2026-04-10 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 394 | 33% | 2021-09-07 |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 34 | 3% | 2015-05-28 |
| 17 other authors | 98 | 8% | all inactive except those in the recent-activity list below |

Every other author owns 16 lines or fewer.

### Per file

| File | Top owner | Next owner |
|---|---|---|
| `lib/index.js` (the library) | Troy 67% | Doug 9%, Alejandro 7% |
| `test/test.js` | Doug 46% | Troy 43% |
| `test/error-response.js` | Troy 86% | Doug 14% |
| `test/example-app.js` | Troy 83% | Doug 17% |
| `test/issue-2.js` | Troy 83% | Doug 17% |
| `test/vary.js` | Troy 100% | none |
| `test/support/env.js` (2 lines) | Doug 100% | none |

### Bus factor: 1

Troy alone owns more than 50% of the surviving code, so the project-level bus factor is 1. Troy is also the only large owner who is still active.

- **Troy Goode:** active, with commits as recently as 2026-04-10. He owns 67% of `lib/index.js`.
- **Douglas Christopher Wilson:** last commit was 5 years ago. He owns 33% of the code, mostly the tests. If you take Troy out, Doug is the next-largest owner, and he is inactive.
- **Recently active contributors:** Jon Church, Ulises Gascón, Ignacio Mangas and dependabot. None of them owns more than a few lines.

### Caveats

- **Commit counts disagree.** Doug has the most commits (143, against Troy's 120). He owns far less of the code that remains, because much of his work has since been rewritten.
- **Sampling and importance checks:** I analysed every file, not a sample. I skipped the import-count check because there are only 2 source directories and `lib/index.js` is the sole library file.
- **Non-JS files are excluded:** the README, package.json, CI config and similar files are not counted.
- **`-M -C` can misattribute moved code.** It follows lines across files, and in a small repo it can credit them to the original author.

If you want, I can break out ownership of `lib/index.js` by function.

